# `dist/` is committed on purpose — a consumer pulling this in as a git
# dependency builds from what is here — so it has to compare cleanly against a
# fresh build, and it did not.
#
# tsc writes LF, and the blobs in the index are LF. But this machine has
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so a checkout wrote them back out as CRLF, and the next
# build overwrote that with LF again. The whole directory then showed as
# modified with an empty diff: content identical, endings not.
#
# It surfaced on any `npm install` in a consumer, not just a deliberate build —
# a symlinked `file:` dependency runs its own `prepare`, so app-server's installs
# were rebuilding this in place and leaving it looking like a stale dist.
#
# Pinning the checkout to LF is the fix: the working copy now matches both the
# index and what the compiler emits, so the round-trip is stable.
dist/** text eol=lf
